                <pb facs="0757" n="655" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg655"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2151/293.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Spanish Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-12-19"><hi rendition="#italic">December 19,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: I beg to advise you, in
                    confirmation of the assurance orally given you on the 17th instant, that, in
                    view of the statements made in your memorandum of the same date, which you left
                    at the department, telegraphic instructions were sent on the 17th instant to the
                    American minister at Tangier directing him to inform th dean of the diplomatic
                    corps that the Government of the United States accepted the assurances given by
                    Mulai Hafid and acquiesced in the concurrent notification of his recognition as
                    Sultan.</p>
                <p>I am, my dear Mr. Minister, very sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
